void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Plaintext alpha("alpha");
  Plaintext one("one");
  Plaintext c0("c0");
  Plaintext c1("c1");
  Plaintext c3("c3");
  Plaintext c5("c5");
  Ciphertext x2 = square(x);
  Ciphertext s = x2 * alpha;
  Ciphertext s3 = s - one;
  s3 = s3 - one;
  s3 = s3 - one;
  Ciphertext s5 = s3 - one;
  s5 = s5 - one;
  Ciphertext r = s * s5;
  Ciphertext r5 = r + one;
  r5 = r5 + one;
  r5 = r5 + one;
  r5 = r5 + one;
  r5 = r5 + one;
  Ciphertext g = r5 * c5 + s3 * c3;
  g = g + c1;
  Ciphertext z = x * alpha;
  Ciphertext y = z * g;
  y = y + c0;
  y.set_output("y");
}
```

This version removes one plaintext multiply. Let s = 4z². Then g = c5·(s²−5s+5) + c3·(s−3) + c1 = (s−3)·(c5·(s−2) + c3) + c1 − c5. The `c3` multiply disappears, and `c1 − c5` is two plaintext adds instead. The depth stays at 5. I haven't timed it.

